{% section id="log" title="Decisions / Deviations Log" %}
- 2026-07-29: Plan created from the fifteen settled decisions and the agreed test-case spec in `92db6890-19c0-497e-a549-a2d3101a005e`. Phasing is dependency-first then risk-ascending: P1 lands the dot that P2 and P3 need, additive work precedes appearance changes, deletions come last, and the one phase with cross-repo blast radius (P4) is isolated with a downstream gate.
- 2026-07-29: P7 is blocked on the T2 branch and one step of P4 is blocked on the D9 scope. Everything else is executable, which is why release after P6 with P7 as a follow-up is recommended.
- 2026-07-29: Branch is `claude/panel-templates-design-system-baa007` on `Nodaste-Lab/weft`, currently local-only with the template layer uncommitted in the working tree.
{% /section %}

{% section id="resume" title="Resume Instructions (Agent)" %}
Read this plan and the decisions plan (`92db6890-19c0-497e-a549-a2d3101a005e`) fully before touching code — the decisions there are settled and this plan may not contradict them. Then inspect the first unchecked Progress item. Write the phase's failing tests before its implementation; the GUARD cases are the contract, not a follow-up. Do not start P7 until the T2 branch is chosen, and do not start P4 step 3 until the D9 scope is answered. Never run a blanket `--update-snapshots` — review each moved baseline in light, dark and compact. Keep `css/weft.css` a pure token file and additive. After each phase, update the matching Progress checkbox and append a dated log line with what moved and what the gates said.
{% /section %}
